            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reconstruction of the microtic ear is one of the most challenging, yet gratifying surgical experiences. Careful planning, attention to detail, and conservative tissue management are necessary for excellent results. Technologies continue to evolve; with the advancement of cartilage tissue engineering, the future of ear reconstruction is very promising.</AbstractText>
